<%# Gmail needs a Google Workspace admin's OK. Mounted by the modal host's
    <template x-if="...id === 'gmail-admin'"> (layouts/application) — single root.

    Gmail read (gmail.readonly) is a RESTRICTED Google scope: Google lets an app
    read mail only after a security assessment, or when the account's Workspace
    admin marks the app's OAuth client Trusted. The hub takes the second road, so
    a signed-in user's Gmail Connect, and Connect Google while Gmail is still
    missing (integrations/_google_connection, _google_connect_all), open this
    first instead of going straight to Google.

    Open it with:
      $store.modals.open('gmail-admin', { href: '<connect path>', clientId: '<id or blank>' })

    props.href     — the connect route the button would have followed (own or
                     household path, already chosen by the server). Continue goes there.
    props.clientId — GoogleConnect::OAuthClient.client_id: the public OAuth
                     client id, never a secret. Blank hides the id row and copy.
    props.ariaLabel — GmailAdminModalHelper::TITLE, the heading below: the modal host
                     names the dialog from it, so a screen reader announces the
                     title rather than the bare id "gmail-admin".

    Continue to Google stays in view: the button row is sticky to the bottom of
    the host's scrolling card, so on a 375px phone it shows without scrolling
    while the steps above scroll behind it.
    No Alpine component of its own and no inline <script>: props come straight from $store.modals, and
    the mailto and the copy (navigator.clipboard) are app/javascript/gmail_admin_modal.js. %>
<div class="text-left" data-test="gmail-admin-modal">
  <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
    <h3 class="text-heading font-bold text-xl"><%= GmailAdminModalHelper::TITLE %></h3>
    <button type="button" @click="$store.modals.close()" class="text-muted hover:text-heading -mt-1" aria-label="Close" data-test="gmail-admin-close">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"/></svg>
    </button>
  </div>

  <p class="text-secondary text-sm">
    Google lets an app read mail only after a security review, or when your company's Google Workspace admin trusts the app.
    So your admin approves McRitchie Studio once, for your whole company, and then anyone there can connect Gmail.
  </p>

  <p class="text-heading text-sm font-medium mt-4 mb-2">For your admin</p>
  <%# Numbered divs, not <ol>/<li>: the layout carries this template on every page, and a page test counting its own "ol li" would count these too. %>
  <div role="list" class="space-y-1 text-sm text-body" data-test="gmail-admin-steps">
    <div role="listitem" class="flex gap-2" data-test="gmail-admin-step"><span class="shrink-0 text-muted">1.</span><span>Sign in to <a href="https://admin.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary hover:underline">admin.google.com</a>.</span></div>
    <div role="listitem" class="flex gap-2" data-test="gmail-admin-step"><span class="shrink-0 text-muted">2.</span><span>Go to Security → Access and data control → API controls → Manage Third-Party App Access → Configure new app.</span></div>
    <div role="listitem" class="flex gap-2" data-test="gmail-admin-step"><span class="shrink-0 text-muted">3.</span><span>Search for the client ID below and select McRitchie Studio.</span></div>
    <div role="listitem" class="flex gap-2" data-test="gmail-admin-step"><span class="shrink-0 text-muted">4.</span><span>Choose Trusted.</span></div>
  </div>

  <template x-if="($store.modals.current().props || {}).clientId">
    <div class="mt-4" data-test="gmail-admin-client">
      <p class="text-xs text-muted mb-1">OAuth client ID</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <code class="min-w-0 flex-1 rounded-lg border border-subtle bg-surface-alt px-2 py-1.5 text-xs text-heading [overflow-wrap:anywhere]" data-test="gmail-admin-client-id" x-text="($store.modals.current().props || {}).clientId"></code>
        <button type="button" @click="window.GmailAdmin.copy($el, ($store.modals.current().props || {}).clientId)" class="btn btn-neutral btn-sm shrink-0" data-test="gmail-admin-copy">
          <span data-copy-label>Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </template>

  <a :href="window.GmailAdmin.mailto(($store.modals.current().props || {}).clientId)" class="btn btn-neutral btn-sm w-full justify-center mt-4" data-test="gmail-admin-email">Email my admin</a>

  <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-3" data-test="gmail-admin-personal">A personal @gmail.com account has no admin, so it can't connect Gmail yet.</p>

  <div class="sticky -bottom-6 -mx-6 -mb-6 mt-5 flex flex-col-reverse gap-2 border-t border-subtle bg-surface px-6 pb-6 pt-4 sm:flex-row sm:justify-end" data-test="gmail-admin-actions">
    <button type="button" @click="$store.modals.close()" class="btn btn-neutral btn-lg justify-center" data-test="gmail-admin-not-now">Not now</button>
    <a :href="($store.modals.current().props || {}).href" data-turbo="false" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg justify-center" data-test="gmail-admin-continue">Continue to Google</a>
  </div>
</div>
